  "notes": "The sheet defines the norm torus V_K and formulates four equivalent conditions on a quotient V′, involving units, a module, a compact real torus, and the largest Weilian subfield. It begins the comparisons and cites Chevalley by name. The sequence continues on scan 143; scan 142 is an inserted lemma sheet. The proof says T′ is majoré par V/Fbar, exactly as written. The deleted map ends at T_K, and its parenthetical clause still mentions V_K mapping into V_L; the opposed directions remain in the cancelled draft. The real-points quotient equality has V′ on the left and V_R(R) on the right. No equivalence theorem was proved in this pass. The overwritten T/V and the bar over E_m were decided from the strokes, with the quotient notation as a consistency cue. Circled §1 and archive number 140 are present.",
